---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const facts = [
  { label: 'Maintainers', value: 'One: Craig Merry. There is no board, no co-founders, no endorsing organizations and no partners yet.' },
  { label: 'Verification', value: 'No third-party verification of the specification, the conformance suite or any implementation.' },
  { label: 'Licenses', value: 'Specification text CC BY 4.0. Reference SDKs (rcan-py, rcan-ts) MIT. Anyone can implement, fork or audit without permission.' },
  { label: 'Neutral steward', value: 'Proposed, not in place. RCAN, with the Robot Registry Foundation registry, has been proposed to the AAIF (Linux Foundation) as a Sandbox project. The proposal has not been accepted.' },
  { label: 'Standards', value: 'Seeking review and collaboration from standards bodies and testing labs. No standards body has endorsed, adopted or approved RCAN.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Governance"
  description="Who maintains RCAN, how it is licensed, its conflicts of interest, and the proposal to move it to a neutral steward."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">

    <!-- Hero -->
    <div class="mb-16">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/20 text-amber-400 text-sm font-medium mb-6">
        Governance status
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-text mb-6 leading-tight">
        Open specification,<br/>
        <span class="text-accent">single maintainer, for now</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        RCAN is an open specification maintained by one person. The goal is to hand it to a neutral steward.
        This page says where that stands, without rounding up.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Facts -->
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mb-6">Where things stand</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-4">
        {facts.map(item => (
          <div class="bg-bg-card border border-border rounded-xl p-5">
            <div class="text-xs font-bold text-text-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">{item.label}</div>
            <div class="text-text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">{item.value}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-4">
        AAIF proposal:
        <a href="https://github.com/aaif/project-proposals/issues/43" class="text-accent hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">aaif/project-proposals#43</a>.
        The physical-assurance test method (Appendix C) is to be presented at the ITU-T FG-EAI workshop on embodied AI,
        16 October 2026 (remote). That is a presentation, not an endorsement.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Conflicts -->
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mb-4">Conflicts of interest</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
        The maintainer also builds <a href="https://opencastor.com" class="text-accent hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenCastor</a>,
        an open-source runtime that implements RCAN, and runs the
        <a href="https://robotregistryfoundation.org" class="text-accent hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Robot Registry Foundation</a> registry.
        OpenCastor is one implementation of RCAN, not the reference for it. Protocol changes are proposed and discussed in public on GitHub.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        The Robot Registry Foundation is likewise proposed, not incorporated. Its draft charter is at
        <a href="https://docs.robotregistryfoundation.org/governance/" class="text-accent hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">docs.robotregistryfoundation.org/governance</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Conformance -->
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mb-4">Conformance is not certification</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
        RCAN defines protocol conformance levels L1–L4. Conformance is self-asserted, and only L1 has an executable
        live checker today. There is no certification program and no certification badge. Certification requires
        audit by a qualified third-party body, which is out of scope for this project.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        Physical assurance levels BE-1 to BE-3 (Appendix C, informative) are a separate axis from L1–L4. An L3 robot can be BE-1.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Get Involved -->
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mb-4">How to get involved</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Review is the most useful contribution: standards bodies, testing labs, academics and implementers who can
        check the spec against their own practice.
      </p>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/RobotRegistryFoundation/rcan-spec"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="group flex flex-col gap-3 bg-bg-card border border-border hover:border-white/20 rounded-xl p-6 transition-colors"
        >
          <span class="font-semibold text-text">RobotRegistryFoundation/rcan-spec</span>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Open issues, review proposals, and comment on changes.</p>
        </a>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 bg-bg-card border border-border rounded-xl p-6">
          <span class="font-semibold text-text">Review and collaboration</span>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">
            Standards bodies and testing labs: contact
            <a href="mailto:foundation@opencastor.ai" class="text-accent hover:underline">foundation@opencastor.ai</a>
            with your affiliation and what you would like to review.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Footer nav -->
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-8 border-t border-border">
      <a href="https://docs.rcan.dev/spec/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 bg-accent text-bg font-bold rounded-lg hover:bg-accent-hover transition-colors text-sm">
        Read the Spec →
      </a>
      <a href="/conformance/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 bg-bg-alt text-text border border-border font-semibold rounded-lg hover:border-white/20 transition-colors text-sm">
        Conformance Levels
      </a>
      <a href="/about" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 bg-bg-alt text-text border border-border font-semibold rounded-lg hover:border-white/20 transition-colors text-sm">
        About RCAN
      </a>
    </div>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
